{"id":"pad","cards":[{"id":"pad445688d6","l":2,"f":"The most important <b>modifiable major</b> risk factor among the options","b":"<b>diabetes mellitus</b> (obesity is minor; family history and male sex aren't modifiable)","c":"Atherosclerosis: Pathophysiology"},{"id":"paddb2e296e","l":1,"f":"<b>Level of arterial disease</b> — list them","b":"<b>Aortoiliac / common iliac</b> · <b>External iliac / proximal femoral</b> · <b>More distal disease</b>","c":"Clinical Presentation"},{"id":"padd0e46ce7","l":1,"f":"<b>Claudication site</b> — list them","b":"<b>Buttock / gluteal</b> · <b>Thigh</b> (or more distal muscles) · <b>Calf / leg</b>","c":"Clinical Presentation"},{"id":"padaf820357","l":1,"f":"<b>Why</b> — list them","b":"Lesion lies above the internal iliac origin → gluteal muscles under-perfused · Internal iliac supply is intact → <b>gluteal perfusion may</b> <b>be preserved</b> · Only the distal muscle territory is ischemic","c":"Clinical Presentation"},{"id":"padd12f0a60","l":1,"f":"<b>Vascular claudication</b> — Cause?","b":"Insufficient arterial supply to exercising muscle","c":"Clinical Presentation"},{"id":"pad31513dd8","l":1,"f":"<b>Neurogenic claudication</b> — Cause?","b":"<b>Neural compression</b>","c":"Clinical Presentation"},{"id":"padba7ced5c","l":1,"f":"<b>Vascular claudication</b> — Pattern?","b":"<b>Reproducible exertional</b> pain","c":"Clinical Presentation"},{"id":"padb3436e30","l":1,"f":"<b>Neurogenic claudication</b> — Pattern?","b":"Often <b>affected by posture</b>","c":"Clinical Presentation"},{"id":"pad7490de22","l":1,"f":"<b>Vascular claudication</b> — Relief?","b":"<b>Stopping / rest</b> — no change of position needed","c":"Clinical Presentation"},{"id":"pad26a7c015","l":1,"f":"<b>Neurogenic claudication</b> — Relief?","b":"May need <b>sitting or spinal flexion</b>","c":"Clinical Presentation"},{"id":"pad254f4bc6","l":2,"f":"Diabetic, leg pain and numbness after <b>500 m</b>, must <b>stop and rest</b> to relieve it, normal neuro exam","b":"<b>vascular claudication</b>","c":"Clinical Presentation"},{"id":"pad632d2755","l":1,"f":"<b>Elevation pallor</b> — What you see?","b":"Foot turns <b>pale</b> when the leg is raised","c":"Physical Examination"},{"id":"padcdb37161","l":1,"f":"<b>Elevation pallor</b> — Mechanism / meaning?","b":"Inadequate arterial perfusion","c":"Physical Examination"},{"id":"padbc7a686f","l":1,"f":"<b>Dependent rubor</b> — What you see?","b":"Foot turns <b>red</b> when lowered","c":"Physical Examination"},{"id":"padcfce931a","l":1,"f":"<b>Dependent rubor</b> — Mechanism / meaning?","b":"<b>Dilated ischemic vessels</b> + increased dependent blood filling","c":"Physical Examination"},{"id":"pad21d27863","l":1,"f":"<b>Ulcer</b> — What you see?","b":"Tissue defect with a <b>visible base</b>; may be deep with exposed bone or necrosis","c":"Physical Examination"},{"id":"pade83ee74b","l":1,"f":"<b>Ulcer</b> — Mechanism / meaning?","b":"Tissue loss from chronic ischemia","c":"Physical Examination"},{"id":"pad23b6a3ef","l":1,"f":"<b>Gangrene</b> — What you see?","b":"Tissue <b>necrosis</b>","c":"Physical Examination"},{"id":"pad2b1a5c60","l":1,"f":"<b>Gangrene</b> — Mechanism / meaning?","b":"<b>Advanced</b> ischemic damage","c":"Physical Examination"},{"id":"pad4c65356b","l":1,"f":"<b>Denominator</b> — Rule?","b":"<b>Higher brachial</b> pressure, used for <b>both legs</b>","c":"Investigations"},{"id":"padac8fd04c","l":1,"f":"<b>Denominator</b> — Reason?","b":"Reduces error from a <b>unilateral upper-limb arterial</b> <b>stenosis</b>","c":"Investigations"},{"id":"pada9e5f727","l":1,"f":"<b>Numerator</b> — Rule?","b":"<b>Higher of DP / PT</b> at each ankle","c":"Investigations"},{"id":"pad8a9bd967","l":1,"f":"<b>Numerator</b> — Reason?","b":"One numerator per leg","c":"Investigations"},{"id":"padd9818965","l":1,"f":"<b>Result</b> — Rule?","b":"<b>Separate right and left ABIs</b>","c":"Investigations"},{"id":"padfee958e5","l":1,"f":"<b>Result</b> — Reason?","b":"Don't simply divide right ankle by right arm","c":"Investigations"},{"id":"paddc8f8830","l":1,"f":"<b>&gt; 1.40</b> — Meaning?","b":"<b>Non-compressible (calcified) arteries</b> — falsely high, not \"excellent perfusion\" (values of ~1.5, sometimes approaching 2)","c":"Investigations"},{"id":"pad3d4df447","l":1,"f":"<b>1.00 – 1.40</b> — Meaning?","b":"Normal","c":"Investigations"},{"id":"pad0b40bebc","l":1,"f":"<b>0.91 – 0.99</b> — Meaning?","b":"Borderline","c":"Investigations"},{"id":"padc91259d0","l":1,"f":"<b>≤ 0.90</b> — Meaning?","b":"<b>PAD</b> — the <b>lower the ABI</b>, the more severe the disease and the <b>worse the cardiovascular risk</b>","c":"Investigations"},{"id":"padc19d56cf","l":1,"f":"<b>guideline values — check them against your lecture slides.</b> — Meaning?","b":"<i>Your notes were cut off at the start of this list (only the \"~1.5, sometimes approaching 2\" fragment survived), so these cut-offs are the standard</i> <i>guideline values — check them against your lecture slides.</i>","c":"Investigations"},{"id":"padc75157a2","l":2,"f":"How to calculate the ABI","b":"<b>ankle systolic BP / brachial systolic BP</b>","c":"Investigations"},{"id":"pad800b8e42","l":1,"f":"<b>Duplex US / colour Doppler</b> — Shows?","b":"Structure (US) + <b>flow</b> <b>velocity &amp; waveforms</b> (Doppler) → anatomy <b>and</b> hemodynamics","c":"Investigations"},{"id":"padfaf11745","l":1,"f":"<b>CT angiography</b> — Shows?","b":"Detailed, standardized anatomy; <b>3D</b> <b>reconstruction</b>","c":"Investigations"},{"id":"pad37413a8b","l":1,"f":"<b>MR angiography</b> — Shows?","b":"Arterial anatomy","c":"Investigations"},{"id":"padf00a125a","l":1,"f":"<b>Catheter angiography</b> — Shows?","b":"Stenosis / occlusion and distal flow","c":"Investigations"},{"id":"pad78be8b85","l":1,"f":"<b>Duplex US / colour Doppler</b> — Radiation / contrast?","b":"<b>Neither</b>","c":"Investigations"},{"id":"pad23791d1f","l":1,"f":"<b>CT angiography</b> — Radiation / contrast?","b":"<b>Radiation + IV contrast</b> (needs IV access)","c":"Investigations"},{"id":"padeb808fda","l":1,"f":"<b>MR angiography</b> — Radiation / contrast?","b":"<b>No ionizing radiation</b>","c":"Investigations"},{"id":"pade76f6ec8","l":1,"f":"<b>Catheter angiography</b> — Radiation / contrast?","b":"<b>Invasive</b> arterial access","c":"Investigations"},{"id":"pad872ad3fe","l":1,"f":"<b>Duplex US / colour Doppler</b> — Practicalities?","b":"Inexpensive, painless, few consumables","c":"Investigations"},{"id":"pad817a85f3","l":1,"f":"<b>CT angiography</b> — Practicalities?","b":"<b>Rapid</b> (~5 min); less operator-dependent","c":"Investigations"},{"id":"pade1ffdc2e","l":1,"f":"<b>MR angiography</b> — Practicalities?","b":"<b>Expensive, slow</b> (often ≥ 30 min), motion- sensitive","c":"Investigations"},{"id":"pad4b37508c","l":1,"f":"<b>Catheter angiography</b> — Practicalities?","b":"Procedure-based","c":"Investigations"},{"id":"pad980b8af6","l":1,"f":"<b>Duplex US / colour Doppler</b> — Main limitation?","b":"<b>Operator-dependent</b> (probe position, angle, visualization)","c":"Investigations"},{"id":"padb57799f6","l":1,"f":"<b>CT angiography</b> — Main limitation?","b":"Contrast and radiation exposure","c":"Investigations"},{"id":"padd27ab453","l":1,"f":"<b>MR angiography</b> — Main limitation?","b":"Less practical in some patients","c":"Investigations"},{"id":"pada0144f6e","l":1,"f":"<b>Catheter angiography</b> — Main limitation?","b":"Invasive","c":"Investigations"},{"id":"pad1d326522","l":1,"f":"<b>Duplex US / colour Doppler</b> — Best use?","b":"Clarify uncertain findings; characterize disease","c":"Investigations"},{"id":"pada448ffa4","l":1,"f":"<b>CT angiography</b> — Best use?","b":"<b>Planning</b> <b>revascularization</b>; extensive assessment","c":"Investigations"},{"id":"pad645b3f80","l":1,"f":"<b>MR angiography</b> — Best use?","b":"Imaging without radiation","c":"Investigations"},{"id":"pad3d0f0014","l":1,"f":"<b>Catheter angiography</b> — Best use?","b":"When an <b>endovascular</b> <b>procedure is planned</b>","c":"Investigations"},{"id":"pad0e99904a","l":2,"f":"Most common cause of <b>calf claudication in a 20-year-old non-smoker</b>","b":"<b>popliteal entrapment syndrome</b>","c":"Relevant Arterial Anatomy"},{"id":"padc432a77d","l":2,"f":"What decreases mortality/progression in <b>Buerger's disease</b>","b":"<b>smoking cessation</b>","c":"PAD Management"},{"id":"pad38fa8fb8","l":2,"f":"Bypass rather than conservative management","b":"<b>rest pain with gangrene of the toes</b> (CLTI) — not claudication &gt; 100 m, not a well-perfused or neuropathic ulcer","c":"Revascularization"},{"id":"pad5484d9b6","l":2,"f":"Surgical rather than conservative","b":"<b>rest pain with gangrene of the toe</b> (fragmentary recall)","c":"Revascularization"},{"id":"padc07c6017","l":2,"f":"Diabetic with a <b>1 × 2 cm forefoot ulcer</b> and pain → keyed <b>wound care and revascularization</b> (both accepted); besides wound care, the most important step","b":"<b>revascularization</b>","c":"Revascularization"},{"id":"pad800e5fc3","l":1,"f":"<b>Endovascular (angioplasty ± stent)</b> — Best suited?","b":"<b>Short / focal</b> lesions","c":"Revascularization"},{"id":"padfa2dcd68","l":1,"f":"<b>Surgical bypass</b> — Best suited?","b":"<b>Long / complex</b> lesions; unfavourable anatomy; <b>failed endovascular</b>","c":"Revascularization"},{"id":"padc15f78db","l":1,"f":"<b>Endovascular (angioplasty ± stent)</b> — Invasiveness?","b":"Lower","c":"Revascularization"},{"id":"pad347c3723","l":1,"f":"<b>Surgical bypass</b> — Invasiveness?","b":"Higher — more incisions","c":"Revascularization"},{"id":"pad2dd5a031","l":1,"f":"<b>Endovascular (angioplasty ± stent)</b> — Procedural risk?","b":"Lower","c":"Revascularization"},{"id":"padab4e7b06","l":1,"f":"<b>Surgical bypass</b> — Procedural risk?","b":"Higher perioperative risk","c":"Revascularization"},{"id":"pad13bd6053","l":1,"f":"<b>Endovascular (angioplasty ± stent)</b> — Recovery?","b":"Faster","c":"Revascularization"},{"id":"padb450897a","l":1,"f":"<b>Surgical bypass</b> — Recovery?","b":"Slower","c":"Revascularization"},{"id":"pad4c93cbdb","l":1,"f":"<b>Endovascular (angioplasty ± stent)</b> — Long-term durability?","b":"<b>Often lower</b> — restenosis / reocclusion, repeat intervention","c":"Revascularization"},{"id":"padca03a150","l":1,"f":"<b>Surgical bypass</b> — Long-term durability?","b":"<b>Often higher</b>, especially with an <b>autologous vein</b> graft","c":"Revascularization"},{"id":"pad0abd40a7","l":1,"f":"<b>Potassium + acids / lactate</b> — Systemic consequence?","b":"<b>Hyperkalemia</b> and <b>metabolic acidosis</b> → <b>cardiac arrhythmias</b>","c":"Irreversible Ischemia & Amputation"},{"id":"paddd07993c","l":1,"f":"<b>Myoglobin</b> — Systemic consequence?","b":"<b>Acute kidney injury</b>","c":"Irreversible Ischemia & Amputation"},{"id":"pad206507c0","l":1,"f":"<b>Toxic metabolites</b> — Systemic consequence?","b":"<b>ARDS</b> and systemic instability","c":"Irreversible Ischemia & Amputation"},{"id":"padba1872ce","l":2,"f":"Sign supporting a non-healing <b>ischaemic</b> ulcer","b":"<b>between the 1st and 2nd toes, tender, with poor granulation tissue</b>","c":"Irreversible Ischemia & Amputation"},{"id":"pad6441e9fa","l":2,"f":"Calf claudication at 500 m, palpable femoral pulse, absent pulses below","b":"next vascular test <b>ankle–brachial index</b>","c":"Mastery Checklist"},{"id":"pad3599f710","l":2,"f":"Calf claudication relieved by rest, <b>ABI 0.60/0.65</b>","b":"<b>best medical therapy and supervised exercise</b> first","c":"Mastery Checklist"}]}